RUNG 5 — found-as: what each string was found as, flattened
  ["10.2.14.7", "ip"]. Friendly and lossy: the vocabulary is dropped, so IT's host and the
  party plan's host come out as one word.

  usage:  5-found-as FILE.eoe ...          every string and its words
          5-found-as ip FILE.eoe ...       only the ips

for each sense marked <NOUN>:                         a sense is [vocabulary, word]
    for each line touching the sense:
        finder = the line at its other end
        if finder is a contains line, or the root's line into a file:
            emit [finder.right, sense's word]          the string it found, and the word

print the pairs, once each, sorted            (only those for the words asked, if any)
